Sureśvarācārya
disciple of Śaṅkarācārya. ment. by Madhusūdana Sarasvatī in his C. Siddhāntabindu on Daśaślokī of Śaṅkarācārya, IO. 2282; by Nīlakaṇṭha in his Vedāntakataka, IO. 2402; by Bhānudatta in his Rasataraṅgiṇī, IO. 1211; by Saccidānanda Bhāratī in his Guruśataka, IO. 3964;
He is also identified with Maṇḍana Miśra an. Viśvarūpa. for details see R. Thangaswami, Bibl. of Adv. Lit. p.. 208. 229; also (diff. from Maṇḍana Miśra) M. Hiriyana, Sureśvara an. Maṇḍana Miśra, JRAS. 1923, p.. 259-63; 1924, p.. 96-97; also Kane, HDS. I. ii. p. 1238b; also see P. Mīm. p. 31. [Page358-b]
